<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Fleetwood buys Western Portables.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Fleetwood buys Western Portables.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fleetwood Corp Ltd said on Tuesday it would buy Western Portables, a maker of transportable accommodation units for the mining industry, for A$12.0 million.</p>
<p>The company said the payment would consist of an issue ot three million fully paid Fleetwood shares to the vendors at A$1.50 each and the remainder would be paid in cash.</p>
<p>Western Portables has an estimated 40 percent of the Western Australian market, it said. The purchase would have a positive impact on earnings per share and lead to overall operating revenue of more than A$65 million in 1996/97.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
